From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: media: cedrus: h265: the collocated picture must be in the active reference list

With temporal MV prediction the engine takes the collocated picture from
its reference list in SRAM: entry collocated_ref_idx of list 0 (always
for a P slice) or of list 1. The driver wrote collocated_ref_idx into
SLICE_HDR_INFO0 unchecked, the V4L2 core does not check it either, and
the job writes the lists only up to their active end; past it stand the
entries of an earlier job. A damaged stream passed on unchecked - a P
slice with num_ref_idx_l0_active_minus1 = 0 and collocated_ref_idx = 3 -
would make the engine read the MV columns of a picture this job does not
hold, or of a buffer already freed: wrong motion, or an IOMMU read fault
and the watchdog.

A valid stream keeps collocated_ref_idx within the list's active entries
(H.265 7.4.7.1). Like an out-of-range reference index (0309), a job
outside that is refused with -EINVAL before the engine is touched. In
range, the entry is one 0309's check has passed.
---
 .../staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h265.c  | 28 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h265.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h265.c
index 3f7c51c52..b872aed94 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h265.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h265.c
@@ -451,6 +451,31 @@ static int cedrus_h265_check_ref_list(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx,
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * With temporal MV prediction the engine takes the collocated picture from
+ * the reference list in its SRAM, entry collocated_ref_idx of list 0 (always
+ * for a P slice) or list 1. The job writes those lists only up to their
+ * active end, and past it stand the entries of an earlier job: an index out
+ * of range would read the MV columns of a picture this job does not hold.
+ * In range, the entry is one cedrus_h265_check_ref_list() has checked.
+ */
+static int cedrus_h265_check_collocated(const struct v4l2_ctrl_hevc_slice_params *slice_params)
+{
+	unsigned int max;
+
+	if (slice_params->slice_type == V4L2_HEVC_SLICE_TYPE_I ||
+	    !(slice_params->flags & V4L2_HEVC_SLICE_PARAMS_FLAG_SLICE_TEMPORAL_MVP_ENABLED))
+		return 0;
+
+	if (slice_params->slice_type == V4L2_HEVC_SLICE_TYPE_P ||
+	    slice_params->flags & V4L2_HEVC_SLICE_PARAMS_FLAG_COLLOCATED_FROM_L0)
+		max = slice_params->num_ref_idx_l0_active_minus1;
+	else
+		max = slice_params->num_ref_idx_l1_active_minus1;
+
+	return slice_params->collocated_ref_idx > max ? -EINVAL : 0;
+}
+
 static int cedrus_h265_setup(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx, struct cedrus_run *run)
 {
 	struct cedrus_dev *dev = ctx->dev;
@@ -539,6 +564,9 @@ static int cedrus_h265_setup(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx, struct cedrus_run *run)
 				       decode_params->num_active_dpb_entries))
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+	if (cedrus_h265_check_collocated(slice_params))
+		return -EINVAL;
+
 	/* Activate H265 engine. */
 	cedrus_engine_enable(ctx);
 
